        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"name\":\"Sinigang na Baboy (Pork Sour Soup) for 4\",\"ingredients\":{\"name\":\"Pork belly with bone\",\"amount\":\"700 g\"},\"steps\":[\"In a large pot, place pork with enough water to cover and bring to a boil. Skim off foam, then simmer 45–60 minutes until pork is tender.\",\"Add onion and tomatoes; if using gabi (taro), add it now. Simmer 10–15 minutes until vegetables start softening.\",\"Dissolve tamarind paste in a little hot water (or add sinigang mix) and stir into the pot. Adjust the sourness to taste.\",\"Add daikon radish and taro (if using) and simmer 8–10 minutes until they are tender.\",\"Add eggplants and green beans; simmer until vegetables are just tender.\",\"Season with fish sauce and adjust saltiness. For a milder heat, skip the chili peppers or leave them whole.\",\"Toss in leafy greens (kangkong or bok choy) and cook 1–2 minutes until wilted. Serve hot with steamed rice.\"]}",
          "providerMetadata": {
            "openai": {
              "itemId": "msg_0f880bdb48343c10006a9143f966a487d0b3ab0ddf90451d82"
            }
          }
